<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · South America</p><h1 class="st-title">United Provinces of New Granada</h1><p class="st-meta">1811 CE – 1816 CE · capital Tunja</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A federation of New Granada's provinces during the 'Foolish Fatherland', torn by civil war before the Spanish reconquest of 1816.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>After the revolutions of 1810, delegates of several provinces of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/viceroyalty-of-new-granada">Viceroyalty of New Granada</a> signed an <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/act-of-federation-of-the-united-provinces-of-new-granada">Act of Federation</a> in November 1811, creating the United Provinces of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-granada">New Granada</a>. Its congress sat at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tunja">Tunja</a> and was led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/camilo-torres-tenorio">Camilo Torres</a>. Cartagena declared absolute independence from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> the same month.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The federation left great power to the provinces and quarrelled with the centralist <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/free-and-independent-state-of-cundinamarca">Free and Independent State of Cundinamarca</a>, leading to civil war. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/simon-bolivar">Bolívar</a>, a refugee from <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/venezuela">Venezuela</a>, wrote his <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cartagena-manifesto">Cartagena Manifesto</a> there in 1812 and led campaigns for the federation. In 1814 he captured <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bogota">Bogotá</a> for the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/dutch-republic">United Provinces</a>, which then moved its government there.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pablo-morillo">Pablo Morillo's</a> royalist expedition besieged Cartagena in 1815, starving it into surrender, and took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bogota">Bogotá</a> in May 1816. Leaders such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/camilo-torres-tenorio">Camilo Torres</a> and the scientist <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francisco-jose-de-caldas">Francisco José de Caldas</a> were executed. The period is remembered as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/patria-boba">Patria Boba</a>, the Foolish Fatherland.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/united-provinces-of-new-granada.jpg" alt="United Provinces of New Granada" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: Racso · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_New_Granada_(1811-1814).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1811 CE – 1816 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>republic</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Tunja</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Camilo Torres, José Fernández Madrid</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Roman Catholicism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Spanish</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/colombia">Colombia</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Provincias Unidas de la Nueva Granada</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1814&amp;focus=united-provinces-of-new-granada" aria-label="United Provinces of New Granada on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="2647 1970 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where United Provinces of New Granada lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M2967 2226L2946 2262M2967 2226L2946 2260M2967 2226L4910 989"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M2946 2262h0M2946 2260h0M4910 989h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M2967 2226h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M2967 2226h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Tunja. <a href="/atlas?year=1814&amp;focus=united-provinces-of-new-granada">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
